From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucian Cristian <lucian.cristian@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Mar 2022 19:26:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] do not look for python when cross-compiling

AM_PATH_PYTHON is only needed for clippy, which is built for the host,
and it fails the target configure run on OpenWrt.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenWrt cross-compile setup]
---
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -980,7 +980,6 @@ AC_DEFINE_UNQUOTED([DFLT_NAME], ["$DFLT_
 #
 
 AS_IF([test "$host" = "$build"], [
-  AM_PATH_PYTHON([3])
   AC_CHECK_HEADER([gelf.h], [], [
     AC_MSG_ERROR([libelf headers are required for building clippy.  (Host only when cross-compiling.)])
   ])
